    "status": "present",
    "value": "A file system is given as a nested directory object. Each directory has a name, a list of child directories and a list of files; each file has a name and its content as a list of byte values. The root directory's own name is ignored, so a file's path is '/' followed by the names of the directories below the root and then the file name, joined by '/'. Find every set of two or more files whose contents are exactly the same byte sequence (empty files count as identical to each other). Return these groups as lists of paths; sort the paths inside each group and sort the groups by their first path."
  },
